MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDot_common — shared input for the lambdaDot DEM fixtures
===========================================================================

This is NOT a runnable case. It holds one copy of the input files that are
byte-identical across the five lambdaDot regression fixtures:

    MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotOff
    MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotTemperature
    MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotChemistry
    MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotBoth
    MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotAltInterp

Each of those five directories symlinks these files in, so the fixtures still
run standalone (`./Allrun`) and are still listed one-per-line in
applications/test/regression/cases_yade.list — nothing in the regression
runner knows this directory exists. It carries no entry there itself.

What stays real and per-case, and is therefore where a reviewer should look
for what actually differs between the fixtures:

    constant/lambdaDict            the test parameter (five distinct versions)
    Allrun                         differs by the asserted lambdaDot sign
    reference/postProcessing/      the committed baseline data
    0.orig/                        see below

Only files OpenFOAM never writes to are shared: constant/ and system/ dicts,
plus Allclean, MPI_lambda.py and .foamcli-monitor.toml. (The mesh OpenFOAM
does write under constant/ — constant/polyMesh/ — is generated fresh by
blockMesh on every run and is untracked, so it is not affected.)

0.orig/ is deliberately NOT shared, even though it is identical across the
five cases. A run copies it to 0/ via restore0Dir, which uses `cp -r`; that
preserves symlinks rather than dereferencing them, so setFields writing
porosityF/porosityF0 into 0/ would follow the link and overwrite the shared
copy. Keeping 0.orig/ real per-case makes that impossible by construction.
The general rule: only add a file here if no stage of a run ever writes it.
